-- title:
--   Theorem 4 — the fixed point iterations (2.1) with τ ∈ (0, 2/λmax(AᵀA)) converge to an optimal solution of (1.8)
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal A:\mathbb R^{m\times n}\to\mathbb R^p$ be linear with matrix $A$ ($\mathcal AX=A\,\mathrm{vec}(X)$), let $b\in\mathbb R^p$, $\mu>0$ and $\tau\in(0,2/\lambda_{\max}(A^\top A))$. Write $g(X)=\mathcal A^*(\mathcal A(X)-b)$ and let $S_\nu$ be the matrix shrinkage operator. Let $(X^k)_{k\ge0}$ be generated by the fixed point iterations (2.1) from an arbitrary $X^0\in\mathbb R^{m\times n}$:
--   $$Y^k=X^k-\tau g(X^k),\qquad X^{k+1}=S_{\tau\mu}(Y^k).$$
--   Then there is an optimal solution $X^*\in\mathcal X^*$ of problem (1.8), $\min_X\mu\|X\|_*+\tfrac12\|\mathcal A(X)-b\|_2^2$, such that
--   $$\lim_{k\to\infty}\|X^k-X^*\|_F=0 .$$
--
--   This is the convergence theorem for the fixed point iterations underlying the FPC and FPCA algorithms for nuclear norm regularized matrix rank minimization: the simple two-line scheme of singular value shrinkage after a gradient step reaches an exact minimizer, for every starting point and every step size below $2/\lambda_{\max}(A^\top A)$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The step range is `StepRange τ Aop` ($0<\tau$, $\tau\|\mathcal A\|_2^2<2$; $\|\mathcal A\|_2^2=\lambda_{\max}(A^\top A)$), written without division so that $\mathcal A=0$ is not vacuous. $\mu>0$ is explicit; the paper needs it for $\nu=\tau\mu>0$. The run is the predicate `IsFixedPointRun`, with $X^0$ arbitrary and $S_{\tau\mu}$ the relation `IsShrink`. Neither the nonemptiness of $\mathcal X^*$ nor the boundedness of the iterates is assumed: both are part of what is to be proved. Convergence is in the Frobenius norm, to some optimal $X^*$ chosen after the run.
-- source:
--   Ma, Goldfarb and Chen, Fixed point and Bregman iterative methods for matrix rank minimization, arXiv:0905.1643v2, p. 12, Theorem 4

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_MaGoldfarbFPC_Convergence_Basic

namespace MaGoldfarbFPC.Convergence

open CaiCandesShen.Convergence Filter Topology

/-- Theorem 4, p. 12: for `μ > 0` and `τ ∈ (0, 2/λ_max(AᵀA))`, every sequence `{X^k}`
generated by the fixed point iterations (2.1) from an arbitrary `X⁰` converges in the
Frobenius norm to some optimal solution `X*` of problem (1.8). -/
theorem theorem4 {m n p : ℕ} (Aop : Fin p → Mat m n) (b : Fin p → ℝ) (μ τ : ℝ)
    (hμ : 0 < μ) (hτ : StepRange τ Aop) (X : ℕ → Mat m n)
    (hX : IsFixedPointRun μ τ Aop b X) :
    ∃ Xs : Mat m n, IsOptimal μ Aop b Xs ∧
      Tendsto (fun k => frobNorm (X k - Xs)) atTop (𝓝 0) := by sorry

end MaGoldfarbFPC.Convergence
